                <pb facs="0902" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4044: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dennis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-11-11T18:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">November 11,
                                1926—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 12—12:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>196. Diaz was designated this afternoon at 1 by Congress in joint session of both
                    Houses. All 21 unseated members were admitted; 53 members present, of whom 44
                    voted for Diaz. Liberal members withdrew before vote and stated that they would
                    present memorial tomorrow declaring they considered Sacasa President. Two votes
                    were cast for resolution declaring Solorzano President. Inaugural ceremony to
                    take place Sunday 14th at 4 afternoon which I shall attend.</p>
                <p>Diaz and Cuadra Pasos called at Legation immediately afterwards. Diaz stated he
                    would form a new Cabinet. Repeated to Central American Republics.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dennis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
